cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Semantic Asset Register: a reproducible quality assessment of US federal published vocabularies"
message: "If you use this register or its check catalogue, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Rovai
    given-names: Fabio
    affiliation: "Kampakis and Co Ltd, trading as The Tesseract Academy"
    email: fabio@thetesseractacademy.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/fabio-rovai/semantic-asset-register"
abstract: >-
  An open, re-runnable audit of the machine-readable semantic assets published by
  United States federal agencies. The register harvests each asset from the URL
  its publisher advertises, records the retrieval as a hashed snapshot, and runs
  a catalogue of 25 checks over it. Every check names the authority it derives
  from and declares whether it is normative, meaning a failure violates a
  published specification, or conventional, meaning a failure departs from a
  community practice the publisher never agreed to. Findings are expressed as
  W3C EARL assertions, so that inapplicable checks are recorded as inapplicable
  rather than as failures.
keywords:
  - ontology evaluation
  - ontology quality
  - SKOS
  - OWL
  - linked data
  - open government data
  - EARL
  - semantic web
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-16"
